{"schema_version":"1.8.0","id":"OESA-2026-3298","published":"2026-08-07T02:44:50Z","modified":"2026-08-07T03:00:57.694780585Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-66373"],"summary":"redis security update","details":"Redis is an advanced key-value store. It is often referred to as a dattructure server since keys can contain strings, hashes ,lists, sets anorted sets.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nRedis before 8.8.0, in the unusual case where an authenticated attacker can execute RESTORE, allows remote code execution via a RESTORE payload where the same NACK (pending entry) is referenced by more than one consumer, because deleting both consumers via XGROUP DELCONSUMER leads to a double free. NOTE: this issue exists because of an incomplete fix for CVE-2026-25243.(CVE-2026-66373)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"redis","ecosystem":"openEuler:22.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/redis&distro=openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.2.15-1.oe2203sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["redis-7.2.15-1.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","redis-debuginfo-7.2.15-1.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","redis-debugsource-7.2.15-1.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"src":["redis-7.2.15-1.oe2203sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["redis-7.2.15-1.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","redis-debuginfo-7.2.15-1.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","redis-debugsource-7.2.15-1.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-3298.json"}},{"package":{"name":"redis","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP1","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/redis&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.2.15-1.oe2403sp1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["redis-7.2.15-1.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","redis-debuginfo-7.2.15-1.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","redis-debugsource-7.2.15-1.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm"],"src":["redis-7.2.15-1.oe2403sp1.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["redis-7.2.15-1.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","redis-debuginfo-7.2.15-1.oe2403sp1.x86_64.